rce boat hunter  in uk territorial waters  after eight minutes the mayday call goes  out from the french coast guard acronym  15  man overboard approximately 15 men  overboard all ships in this area are  requested to have a short lookout to  break it to this area they quote these  coordinates  this location is in french territorial  waters but less than a mile from uk  waters the direction of the wind and  currents would have been pushing the  dinghy back towards france  the fact they gave the location is  significant given that the french coast  guard had actually given the specific  location  and had put a mayday call out to  a whole search and rescue area  i would suggest that that is a friend  giving permission to uh  any  vessel in that location in that locality  to enter  french territorial waters to rescue the  dinghy a number of boats including a uk  trawler and four french fishing boats  can be seen here they're within five  miles of the mayday location four  minutes after the mayday call the uk  search and rescue helicopter from lid  lifts it can be seen here  ten minutes later the french coast guard  boat escao launches from dunkirk  at 205 french rescue boat notre dame de  response launches from cali port the  rescue effort continues throughout the  afternoon and into the early evening  but by now it's clear this is a recovery  operation  secretary  the home office says the incident was in  french waters  and the uk coast guard provided help as  soon as it was requested by the french  but experts say where the incident took  place is not relevant so as far as  rescuing people at sea  uh is concerned  we need to think about  two areas of  the sea one is the peripheral waters and  the other is the search and rescue area  states are responsible for their search  and rescue area and this area can extend  beyond  the parrotborough waters once the french  coast guard put out the mayday call any  uk boats close enough could have helped  unless  they would have 